1
00:00:00,580 --> 00:00:01,860
April fifteenth.

2
00:00:02,100 --> 00:00:04,420
Meera deposits fifteen thousand rupees at

3
00:00:04,500 --> 00:00:05,100
the bank.

4
00:00:05,300 --> 00:00:06,460
Her phone buzzes.

5
00:00:06,740 --> 00:00:09,060
Your account is credited with fifteen thousand

6
00:00:09,140 --> 00:00:09,860
rupees.

7
00:00:10,706 --> 00:00:11,706
Credited!

8
00:00:11,906 --> 00:00:15,266
Credit means money in, and money in is good.

9
00:00:15,426 --> 00:00:16,066
Right?

10
00:00:17,113 --> 00:00:18,513
Khata has news.

11
00:00:18,713 --> 00:00:21,593
In Meera's own books, that same deposit

12
00:00:21,673 --> 00:00:22,713
is a debit.

13
00:00:24,116 --> 00:00:25,636
So who's right?

14
00:00:31,578 --> 00:00:33,778
First, last time's questions.

15
00:00:34,058 --> 00:00:34,778
One.

16
00:00:34,858 --> 00:00:37,178
The four thousand rupee catering advance.

17
00:00:37,258 --> 00:00:38,778
Is it April's revenue?

18
00:00:39,936 --> 00:00:40,536
No.

19
00:00:40,736 --> 00:00:43,456
The stall still owes that customer an event.

20
00:00:43,496 --> 00:00:44,656
It's a liability.

21
00:00:45,211 --> 00:00:45,771
Two.

22
00:00:46,011 --> 00:00:48,611
Paying Gopal Dairy five thousand rupees.

23
00:00:48,811 --> 00:00:50,171
Is that an expense?

24
00:00:51,322 --> 00:00:51,722
No.

25
00:00:52,122 --> 00:00:54,522
Paying Gopal just shrinks what the stall

26
00:00:54,602 --> 00:00:55,322
owes him.

27
00:00:55,893 --> 00:00:56,573
Three.

28
00:00:56,853 --> 00:00:59,653
After Infotech pays four thousand, how much

29
00:00:59,733 --> 00:01:00,933
do they still owe?

30
00:01:02,082 --> 00:01:03,282
Two thousand.

31
00:01:03,362 --> 00:01:06,242
Six thousand billed, four thousand paid.

32
00:01:07,010 --> 00:01:08,610
And Aman's samosa challenge?

33
00:01:08,690 --> 00:01:11,570
Only the cash sale and the rent moved both

34
00:01:11,650 --> 00:01:12,330
needles.

35
00:01:12,610 --> 00:01:15,250
Aman's profit so far: eight thousand five

36
00:01:15,330 --> 00:01:16,450
hundred rupees.

37
00:01:17,714 --> 00:01:19,554
Now, that SMS.

38
00:01:20,034 --> 00:01:21,874
First, four myths to drop.

39
00:01:22,354 --> 00:01:23,754
Debit isn't bad.

40
00:01:23,954 --> 00:01:25,634
Credit isn't good.

41
00:01:26,114 --> 00:01:28,994
Neither one means money in, or money out.

42
00:01:29,074 --> 00:01:31,714
And neither one means plus, or minus.

43
00:01:32,351 --> 00:01:34,431
So here's what they really mean.

44
00:01:34,471 --> 00:01:37,391
In accounting, debit just means left.

45
00:01:38,111 --> 00:01:39,911
And credit just means right.

46
00:01:40,832 --> 00:01:43,472
Remember Khata's two pages, from the very

47
00:01:43,552 --> 00:01:44,432
first lesson?

48
00:01:44,672 --> 00:01:45,632
This is why.

49
00:01:46,683 --> 00:01:48,363
So which side do you write on?

50
00:01:48,843 --> 00:01:49,883
Look at the scale.

51
00:01:50,123 --> 00:01:51,443
Assets on the left.

52
00:01:51,643 --> 00:01:53,803
Liabilities and equity on the right.

53
00:01:54,203 --> 00:01:56,763
Every account has a home side: the side

54
00:01:56,843 --> 00:01:57,803
where it lives.

55
00:01:58,359 --> 00:01:59,719
And here's the whole rule.

56
00:02:00,199 --> 00:02:02,839
When an account grows, write it on its home

57
00:02:02,919 --> 00:02:03,439
side.

58
00:02:04,239 --> 00:02:06,799
When it shrinks, write it on the other side.

59
00:02:07,848 --> 00:02:09,128
April first.

60
00:02:09,208 --> 00:02:11,688
Meera puts in fifty thousand rupees.

61
00:02:11,808 --> 00:02:13,288
Which two things changed?

62
00:02:15,256 --> 00:02:16,056
Cash went up.

63
00:02:16,136 --> 00:02:18,536
An asset, home on the left.

64
00:02:18,936 --> 00:02:20,136
Debit Cash.

65
00:02:20,876 --> 00:02:21,996
Capital went up.

66
00:02:22,236 --> 00:02:24,076
Equity, home on the right.

67
00:02:24,236 --> 00:02:25,396
Credit Capital.

68
00:02:25,596 --> 00:02:28,236
Fifty thousand left, fifty thousand right.

69
00:02:28,990 --> 00:02:32,030
Now the cart, thirty-six thousand rupees.

70
00:02:32,270 --> 00:02:33,870
Which two things changed?

71
00:02:35,822 --> 00:02:37,222
Equipment grows.

72
00:02:37,422 --> 00:02:39,622
An asset, home on the left.

73
00:02:39,822 --> 00:02:41,102
Debit Equipment.

74
00:02:42,002 --> 00:02:43,642
But Cash shrinks.

75
00:02:43,842 --> 00:02:46,482
Cash lives on the left, so to shrink it,

76
00:02:46,562 --> 00:02:47,562
write on the right.

77
00:02:47,762 --> 00:02:49,122
Credit Cash.

78
00:02:50,670 --> 00:02:53,230
So debit doesn't always mean up.

79
00:02:54,250 --> 00:02:55,610
It depends on the home.

80
00:02:56,876 --> 00:02:59,116
Liabilities work the same way, from the

81
00:02:59,196 --> 00:03:00,076
other side.

82
00:03:00,156 --> 00:03:02,156
Gopal Dairy sends eight thousand rupees

83
00:03:02,236 --> 00:03:03,916
of stock, pay later.

84
00:03:03,996 --> 00:03:05,196
Stock grows.

85
00:03:05,276 --> 00:03:06,476
Debit Stock.

86
00:03:06,556 --> 00:03:07,516
And Gopal?

87
00:03:07,596 --> 00:03:09,036
Debit, or credit?

88
00:03:10,597 --> 00:03:11,317
Credit.

89
00:03:11,557 --> 00:03:14,917
What the stall owes Gopal grew, and liabilities

90
00:03:15,077 --> 00:03:16,037
live on the right.

91
00:03:17,104 --> 00:03:18,224
April fifth.

92
00:03:18,464 --> 00:03:20,464
Rent, five thousand rupees.

93
00:03:20,704 --> 00:03:21,944
Cash shrinks.

94
00:03:22,144 --> 00:03:23,144
Credit Cash.

95
00:03:23,844 --> 00:03:24,604
And Rent?

96
00:03:24,964 --> 00:03:26,164
Rent grew.

97
00:03:26,244 --> 00:03:27,844
But where is its home?

98
00:03:28,592 --> 00:03:30,272
Remember the long equation?

99
00:03:30,512 --> 00:03:33,312
Assets equal liabilities, plus capital,

100
00:03:33,432 --> 00:03:35,872
plus revenue, minus expenses.

101
00:03:36,592 --> 00:03:38,472
That minus is the clue.

102
00:03:38,552 --> 00:03:41,032
Move Expenses across the equals sign, and

103
00:03:41,072 --> 00:03:42,872
the minus becomes a plus.

104
00:03:43,428 --> 00:03:46,708
Assets, plus expenses, equal liabilities,

105
00:03:46,828 --> 00:03:48,948
plus capital, plus revenue.

106
00:03:50,528 --> 00:03:53,248
So expenses live on the left, with the assets.

107
00:03:53,488 --> 00:03:56,128
Rent grew, and the left is its home.

108
00:03:56,288 --> 00:03:57,568
Debit Rent.

109
00:03:58,228 --> 00:03:59,908
Every expense is a debit.

110
00:04:00,673 --> 00:04:03,473
Revenue never moved, so its home stays on

111
00:04:03,553 --> 00:04:05,153
the right, with capital.

112
00:04:05,393 --> 00:04:07,393
Every sale is a credit.

113
00:04:08,461 --> 00:04:09,261
Put it together.

114
00:04:09,741 --> 00:04:12,941
Debits live on the left: Expenses, Assets,

115
00:04:12,981 --> 00:04:15,581
and Drawings, the money Meera takes home.

116
00:04:15,661 --> 00:04:17,341
They behave like expenses.

117
00:04:17,890 --> 00:04:20,570
Credits live on the right: Liabilities,

118
00:04:20,770 --> 00:04:23,650
Income, that's revenue, or income, same

119
00:04:23,770 --> 00:04:25,090
thing, and Capital.

120
00:04:25,570 --> 00:04:27,090
In short: DEAD CLIC.

121
00:04:27,570 --> 00:04:28,850
You didn't memorise this.

122
00:04:29,010 --> 00:04:31,090
You read it straight off the equation.

123
00:04:31,656 --> 00:04:34,456
And in every transaction, the left total

124
00:04:34,696 --> 00:04:36,136
equals the right total.

125
00:04:36,456 --> 00:04:37,176
Always.

126
00:04:37,896 --> 00:04:40,336
That's double entry: every rupee written

127
00:04:40,416 --> 00:04:42,736
twice, once on each side.

128
00:04:42,816 --> 00:04:45,136
The same scale, in a new costume.

129
00:04:46,382 --> 00:04:48,382
So, the SMS.

130
00:04:48,942 --> 00:04:51,182
Two cameras, one deposit.

131
00:04:51,262 --> 00:04:53,822
In Meera's books, money moved from the galla

132
00:04:53,902 --> 00:04:54,862
to the bank.

133
00:04:54,942 --> 00:04:56,142
Bank grows.

134
00:04:56,182 --> 00:04:57,182
Debit Bank.

135
00:04:57,382 --> 00:04:58,382
Cash shrinks.

136
00:04:58,542 --> 00:04:59,662
Credit Cash.

137
00:05:00,226 --> 00:05:02,546
In the bank's books, the notes land in its

138
00:05:02,626 --> 00:05:03,346
vault.

139
00:05:03,426 --> 00:05:04,786
That's its debit.

140
00:05:04,866 --> 00:05:07,266
But Meera's fifteen thousand isn't the bank's

141
00:05:07,346 --> 00:05:07,826
money.

142
00:05:08,066 --> 00:05:10,466
It's money the bank owes her, any day she

143
00:05:10,546 --> 00:05:11,146
asks.

144
00:05:11,346 --> 00:05:13,626
For the bank, that's a liability.

145
00:05:13,826 --> 00:05:16,386
It grows, so the bank credits it.

146
00:05:16,944 --> 00:05:17,664
Same money.

147
00:05:17,744 --> 00:05:19,264
Opposite books.

148
00:05:20,104 --> 00:05:22,904
Your SMS is reading the bank's khata, not

149
00:05:22,984 --> 00:05:23,624
yours.

150
00:05:23,944 --> 00:05:25,704
Credit doesn't mean good.

151
00:05:25,784 --> 00:05:27,704
Debit doesn't mean bad.

152
00:05:27,784 --> 00:05:29,944
They just mean right, and left.

153
00:05:31,280 --> 00:05:32,240
Let's practise.

154
00:05:32,400 --> 00:05:34,920
Warm-up first: one account at a time.

155
00:05:35,120 --> 00:05:35,920
Which side?

156
00:05:36,240 --> 00:05:38,120
Ravi Mama's loan grows.

157
00:05:39,720 --> 00:05:40,360
Credit.

158
00:05:40,600 --> 00:05:41,600
Rent grows.

159
00:05:43,200 --> 00:05:43,800
Debit.

160
00:05:44,000 --> 00:05:44,760
A sale.

161
00:05:46,360 --> 00:05:46,840
Credit.

162
00:05:47,240 --> 00:05:48,120
Now, careful.

163
00:05:48,360 --> 00:05:51,160
Infotech pays what it owes, so the Infotech

164
00:05:51,240 --> 00:05:52,520
account shrinks.

165
00:05:54,480 --> 00:05:55,120
Credit.

166
00:05:55,360 --> 00:05:57,680
An asset shrinking goes on the right.

167
00:05:58,427 --> 00:05:59,627
Now full entries.

168
00:06:00,027 --> 00:06:01,347
Khata goes first.

169
00:06:01,627 --> 00:06:04,027
Cash sales for the first half of April:

170
00:06:04,107 --> 00:06:05,587
eighteen thousand rupees.

171
00:06:05,867 --> 00:06:07,547
Which two things changed?

172
00:06:09,518 --> 00:06:10,238
Cash grew.

173
00:06:10,318 --> 00:06:13,038
Debit Cash, eighteen thousand.

174
00:06:13,118 --> 00:06:14,158
Sales grew.

175
00:06:14,238 --> 00:06:16,798
That's revenue, so credit Sales, eighteen

176
00:06:16,878 --> 00:06:17,758
thousand.

177
00:06:17,838 --> 00:06:19,358
Left equals right.

178
00:06:20,114 --> 00:06:20,914
Meera's turn.

179
00:06:21,394 --> 00:06:24,194
Infotech's chai tab: six thousand rupees,

180
00:06:24,434 --> 00:06:25,154
pay later.

181
00:06:25,394 --> 00:06:28,114
The chai was sold, so credit Sales, six

182
00:06:28,274 --> 00:06:29,154
thousand.

183
00:06:29,234 --> 00:06:30,274
Now Infotech.

184
00:06:30,674 --> 00:06:31,954
They owe the stall.

185
00:06:32,194 --> 00:06:34,114
Meera slides it toward the right page.

186
00:06:34,514 --> 00:06:37,114
Owing money, that was Gopal's side.

187
00:06:37,314 --> 00:06:38,034
Wasn't it?

188
00:06:40,382 --> 00:06:40,782
No.

189
00:06:41,182 --> 00:06:43,022
Gopal is owed by the stall.

190
00:06:43,502 --> 00:06:45,302
Infotech owes the stall.

191
00:06:45,502 --> 00:06:47,182
An asset, and it grew.

192
00:06:47,582 --> 00:06:49,022
Home side, left.

193
00:06:49,262 --> 00:06:51,422
Debit Infotech, six thousand.

194
00:06:52,339 --> 00:06:53,659
Now, just you.

195
00:06:53,939 --> 00:06:56,899
Meera pays Gopal Dairy five thousand rupees.

196
00:06:57,139 --> 00:06:57,899
Debit what?

197
00:06:58,099 --> 00:06:58,979
Credit what?

198
00:07:02,145 --> 00:07:03,585
Debit Gopal Dairy.

199
00:07:04,065 --> 00:07:06,465
The liability shrinks, so it goes on the

200
00:07:06,665 --> 00:07:07,105
left.

201
00:07:07,345 --> 00:07:08,785
Credit Cash.

202
00:07:08,865 --> 00:07:10,705
Five thousand leaves the galla.

203
00:07:11,961 --> 00:07:12,681
So.

204
00:07:12,761 --> 00:07:15,241
Debit is left, credit is right.

205
00:07:15,361 --> 00:07:17,481
Grow an account on its home side, shrink

206
00:07:17,561 --> 00:07:18,681
it on the other.

207
00:07:18,721 --> 00:07:21,321
And the bank's SMS speaks from the bank's

208
00:07:21,561 --> 00:07:22,121
books.

209
00:07:23,330 --> 00:07:23,970
Your turn.

210
00:07:24,130 --> 00:07:25,130
Three quick ones.

211
00:07:25,330 --> 00:07:25,810
One.

212
00:07:26,050 --> 00:07:28,770
Meera buys six thousand rupees of tea, milk

213
00:07:28,850 --> 00:07:30,650
and sugar, and pays cash.

214
00:07:30,850 --> 00:07:32,850
What's debited, and what's credited?

215
00:07:33,410 --> 00:07:33,890
Two.

216
00:07:34,130 --> 00:07:36,210
Why is an expense a debit?

217
00:07:36,530 --> 00:07:37,090
Three.

218
00:07:37,330 --> 00:07:39,410
Imagine Meera pays a bill from the bank,

219
00:07:39,490 --> 00:07:41,330
and the SMS says debited.

220
00:07:41,730 --> 00:07:44,690
In Meera's books, is Bank debited, or credited?

221
00:07:45,170 --> 00:07:46,850
Answers next lesson.

222
00:07:48,271 --> 00:07:50,831
Next time, Meera's CA friend drops by the

223
00:07:50,911 --> 00:07:52,671
stall, with rules.

224
00:07:52,911 --> 00:07:53,951
Debit the receiver!

225
00:07:54,111 --> 00:07:55,191
Credit the giver!

226
00:07:55,391 --> 00:07:57,391
Is that a whole new system to learn?
